*** Keywords ***
Common Suite Setup
    [Documentation]  Prepares testing environment before running test suite. Tries to reach onAir state on all available BTSs (gNB and remote eNB).
    ...              If any preparation step fails or unallowed alarms are detected then logs will be collected and test suite execution will be aborted.
    ...              IMPORTANT! Whenever "gNB" is mentioned here it also includes tested BTS with only LTE RAT configured on it (LTE only).
    ...
    ...              ARGS:
    ...              - commission (bool): defines whether gNB should be commissioned;
    ...                                   defaults to: False (gNB commissioning will not be performed);
    ...                                   recommended value: True
    ...              - commission_lte (bool): defines whether remote eNB from should be commissioned;
    ...                                       defaults to: False (remote eNB commissioning will not be performed);
    ...                                       recommended value: True for NSA mode, False otherwise
    ...              - commission_second_gNB (bool): defines whether secondary gNB should be commissioned;
    ...                                              defaults to: False (secondary gNB commissioning will not be performed);
    ...                                              recommended value: True for RF Sharing config with two gNBs, False otherwise
    ...              - optical_switch_settings (dict or list(dict)): configurations of optical switches to be set before commissioning for gNB site;
    ...                                                              i.e. {"optical_switch_id": 0, "module_number": 1, "output_channel": 2}
    ...                                                              or [{"optical_switch_id": 0, "module_number": 1, "output_channel": 2},
    ...                                                                  {"optical_switch_id": 0, "module_number": 2, "output_channel": 3}]
    ...                                                defaults to: None (optical switch configuration will not be changed);
    ...                                                recommended value: None
    ...              - force_logs_collection (bool): defines whether logs should be collected despite passing test;
    ...                                              defaults to: False (logs will not be collected when test is passing);
    ...                                              recommended value: False
    ...              - btslog (bool): defines whether BTSLog (syslog) should be collected from gNB during suite setup execution;
    ...                               defaults to: True (BTSLog from gNB will be collected);
    ...                               recommended value: True
    ...              - gnb_slave_btslog (bool): defines whether BTSLog (syslog) should be collected from slave part of Fullrack gNB during suite setup execution;
    ...                                         defaults to: False (BTSLog from slave gNB part will not be collected);
    ...                                         recommended value: True for Fullrack configuration, False otherwise
    ...              - remote_enb_btslog (bool): defines whether BTSLog (syslog) should be collected from remote eNB during suite setup execution;
    ...                                          defaults to: False (BTSLog from remote eNB will not be collected);
    ...                                          recommended value: True for NSA mode, False otherwise
    ...              - enable_rmod_logs_to_btslog (bool): defines whether RMOD logs should be sent to BTSLog in real time during test suite execution;
    ...                                                   it will be enabled for RMODs present in current suite setup SCF, please use enable_rmod_logs_to_btslog
    ...                                                   in test setup in case of custom SCF file for specific test;
    ...                                                   defaults to: False (RMOD logs will not be sent to BTSLog);
    ...                                                   recommended value: False
    ...              - enabling_rmod_logs_to_btslog_custom_settings (dict): custom settings for enabling RMOD logs handover to BTSLog,
    ...                                                                     where key is configuration RMOD ID (string) and value is a list with
    ...                                                                     custom rad commands to be executed on RMOD (via FHNET connection)
    ...                                                                     or None if default commands should be used (default values only CPRI and eCPRI RMODs);
    ...                                                                     i.e. {'1': ['rad -mpw 0x10041 2', 'rad -mpw 0x10042 3232300926', 'rad -mpw 0x10043 51000'],
    ...                                                                           '2': ['rad -mpw 0x1003f 1', 'rad -mpw 0x10040 1', 'rad -mpw 0x10041 0x2',
    ...                                                                                 'rad -mpw 0x10042 0xAC150002', 'rad -mpw 0x10043 0xC738', 'rad -mpw 0x10045 0xF00000'],
    ...                                                                           '3': None}
    ...                                                                     defaults to: None (default commands will be used for all RMODs);
    ...                                                                     recommended value: None
    ...              - manual_snapshot (bool): defines whether manual snapshot should be collected via Telnet from gNB;
    ...                                        defaults to: False (manual snapshot will not be collected);
    ...                                        recommended value: False
    ...              - lte_snapshot (bool): defines whether snapshot should be collected from remote eNB;
    ...                                     defaults to: False (snapshot from remote eNB will not be collected);
    ...                                     recommended value: True for NSA mode, False otherwise
    ...              - custom_tl (TestLine): further referenced to as "suite custom init";
    ...                                      replaces testline (tl) configuration from default init (provided via 'robot -V /path/to/init')
    ...                                      with testline configuration from custom init for the duration of entire test suite execution
    ...                                      (unless it is later temporarily replaced by test custom init for the duration of a single test case execution);
    ...                                      suite custom init content must be a subset of default init content if validate_configuration_file is enabled;
    ...                                      if default init consists of RMODs that are not listed in suite custom init,
    ...                                      then those unused RMODs will be powered off during commissioning;
    ...                                      i.e. ${tl_abip_ahgb};
    ...                                      defaults to: None (suite custom init will not be used);
    ...                                      recommended value: None
    ...              - additional_gnb_allowed_alarms (list(str)): fault IDs which should be added to global additional allowed alarms on gNB
    ...                                                           for the duration of entire test suite execution;
    ...                                                           defaults to: None (no additional allowed alarms will be added on gNB);
    ...                                                           recommended value: None
    ...              - additional_enb_allowed_alarms (list(str)): fault IDs which should be added to global additional allowed alarms on remote eNB
    ...                                                           for the duration of entire test suite execution;
    ...                                                           defaults to: None (no additional allowed alarms will be added on remote eNB);
    ...                                                           recommended value: None
    ...              - lmi_interface (bool): defines whether LMI ETH interface should be configured on Test PC;
    ...                                      defaults to: False (LMI interface will not be configured);
    ...                                      recommended value: True
    ...              - power_reset (bool): defines whether power reset of all RMODs and SMODs from gNB and remote eNB (if present) should be performed;
    ...                                    defaults to: False (power reset will not be performed);
    ...                                    recommended value: False
    ...              - check_gnb_lte_sw_match (bool): defines whether matching of SW versions from gNB and remote eNB should be checked;
    ...                                               fails test suite execution if SW versions are not matching;
    ...                                               defaults to: False (SW matching between gNB and remote eNB will not be checked);
    ...                                               recommended value: True for NSA mode, False otherwise
    ...              - remote_path_bsrpackage (str): absolute path to BSR package stored on Appserver;
    ...                                              if provided, then package will be uploaded on gNB BTS;
    ...                                              i.e. /home/ute/UTE5GSISOAUTO025/BSR_AZQS_1_H6_ALN45_ARP45_UCA_00001_00001.zip
    ...                                              defaults to: None (BSR package will not be uploaded);
    ...                                              recommended value: None
    ...              - validate_configuration_file (bool): defines whether content of default init and suite custom init (if used), should be validated;
    ...                                                    additionally, if suite custom init is used, it will be checked, whether its content is a subset of default init content;
    ...                                                    validation must be skipped if testline has simulator (i.e. Airphone);
    ...                                                    defaults to: True (init will be validated);
    ...                                                    recommended value: True for BTS without simulator, False otherwise
    ...              - is_rmod_in_share_mode (bool): must be set to True if any RMOD is being shared between gNB and remote eNB;
    ...                                              defaults to: False (no RMOD sharing between gNB and remote eNB);
    ...                                              recommended value: True if RMOD is being shared between gNB and remote eNB, False otherwise
    ...              - custom_scf_file_path_5g (str): absolute path to custom SCF file for gNB or name of custom SCF file (without .xml extension)
    ...                                               for this testline from gears repository;
    ...                                               if provided it will be used instead of default SCF file for this testline found in robotws repository;
    ...                                               must be provided if testline has simulator (i.e. Airphone) and commissioning should be done;
    ...                                               i.e. ${EXECDIR}/testsuite/Wroclaw/SISO/TestLines/7_16_UTE5GSISOAUTO005/SCF/5G/custom_scf/SCF_SISOAUTO005_SBTS_master_10766.xml
    ...                                               defaults to: None (default SCF file for gNB be used or BTS with simulator will not be commissioned);
    ...                                               recommended value: None for BTS without simulator, SCF file path otherwise
    ...              - custom_scf_file_path_lte (str): absolute path to custom SCF file for remote eNB;
    ...                                                if provided it will be used instead of default SCF file for this testline found in robotws repository;
    ...                                                i.e. ${EXECDIR}/testsuite/Wroclaw/SISO/TestLines/7_16_UTE5GSISOAUTO018/SCF/4G/custom_scf/SCF_SISOAUTO018_LTE_SBTS_uDTX_off.xml
    ...                                                defaults to: None (default SCF file for remote eNB be used);
    ...                                                recommended value: None
    ...              - stop_and_fix_gnb (bool): defines whether stop and fix mechnism should be executed for gNB;
    ...                                         if set to True and truckroll will be detected on gNB then test suite execution will be paused for manual investigation;
    ...                                         defaults to: False (stop and fix for gNB will never be triggered);
    ...                                         recommended value: True
    ...              - stop_and_fix_enb (bool): defines whether stop and fix mechnism should be executed for remote eNB;
    ...                                         if set to True and truckroll will be detected on remote eNB then test suite execution will be paused for manual investigation;
    ...                                         defaults to: False (stop and fix for remote eNB will never be triggered);
    ...                                         recommended value: True for NSA mode, False otherwise
    ...              - name_of_btslog_file (str): custom file name where btslog will be collected;
    ...                                           defaults to: btslog_on_testvm;
    ...                                           recommended value: btslog_on_testvm
    ...              - rmod_logs (bool): defines whether logs from gNB RMODs should be collected - either via LMI (if present) or via FHNET container;
    ...                                  defaults to: False (logs will not be collected from any gNB RMOD);
    ...                                  recommended value: True
    ...              - swconfig_upload (bool): defines whether swconfig file should be uploaded and activated on gNB SMOD;
    ...                                        default swconfig files (i.e. swconfig_SISOAUTO026_SBTS23R3.txt) for this testline shoudld be stored in robotws repository;
    ...                                        defaults to: False (swconfig will not be uploaded on gNB);
    ...                                        recommended value: True if gNB swconfig for this testline is available, False otherwise
    ...              - custom_swconfig_path_gnb (str): name of custom swconfig file from robotws repository or absolute path to custom swconfig file which sholud be uploaded on gNB SMOD;
    ...                                                if None provided then default swconfig file for this testline from robotws repository will be uploaded on gNB SMOD;
    ...                                                requires swconfig_upload set to True to be able to upload swconfig file at all;
    ...                                                i.e. swconfig_AUTO042_24R1.txt (for custom file from robotws) or /home/ute/custom_swconfig.txt (for any custom file) or None (for default file from robotws);
    ...                                                defaults to: None (default swconfig file for this testline from robotws repository will be uploaded on gNB SMOD);
    ...                                                recommended value: None
    ...              - swconfig_upload_remote_lte (bool): defines whether swconfig file should be uploaded and activated on remote eNB SMOD;
    ...                                                   default swconfig files (i.e. swconfig_SISOAUTO026_LTE_SBTS23R3.txt) for this testline shoudld be stored in robotws repository;
    ...                                                   defaults to: False (swconfig will not be uploaded on remote eNB);
    ...                                                   recommended value: True for NSA mode and if remote eNB swconfig for this testline is available, False otherwise
    ...              - custom_swconfig_path_lte (str): name of custom swconfig file from robotws repository or absolute path to custom swconfig file which sholud be uploaded on remote eNB SMOD;
    ...                                                if None provided then default swconfig file for this testline from robotws repository will be uploaded on remote eNB SMOD;
    ...                                                requires swconfig_upload_remote_lte set to True to be able to upload swconfig file at all;
    ...                                                i.e. swconfig_AUTO042_LTE_24R1.txt (for custom file from robotws) or /home/ute/custom_lte_swconfig.txt (for any custom file) or None (for default file from robotws);
    ...                                                defaults to: None (default swconfig file for this testline from robotws repository will be uploaded on remote eNB SMOD);
    ...                                                recommended value: None
    ...              - gnss_update (bool): defines whether GNSS update should be performed on gNB if necessary;
    ...                                    defaults to: True (GNSS update will be performed if there is a mismatch between actual GNSS SW version and GNSS SW version in BTS packages);
    ...                                    recommended value: True
    ...              - custom_rmod_setup_yaml_path (str): absolute path to custom RMOD console connection setup YAML file. If provided, then custom RMOD console connection setup will be used.
    ...                                                   example YAML file can be found under repository path: taf/hw/rf_diagnostic_card/examples/custom_setup_example.yaml;
    ...                                                   Defaults to None (default RMOD console connection setup will be used);
    ...              - iphy_configs (list): A list of dictionaries for configuring IPHY on BTSs with simulators (e.g., Airphone).
    ...                                     Each dictionary in the list represents one simulator configuration and must contain the following keys:
    ...                                     - `ip` (str): The IP address of the simulator instance.
    ...                                     - `remote_host` (str or None): The remote host for the connection, or `${None}` if not applicable.
    ...                                     - `iphy_file` (str): The absolute path to the `iphy.xml` configuration file for that simulator.
    ...                                     Example (can be created using `Evaluate` keyword or from a variable file):
    ...                                     [{'ip': '192.168.1.1',
    ...                                       'remote_host': None,
    ...                                       'iphy_file': 'some_path'},
    ...                                      {'ip': '192.168.1.129',
    ...                                       'remote_host': '10.2.1.15',
    ...                                       'iphy_file': 'some_path2'}]
    ...                                     Defaults to: `${None}` (IPHY file uploading will be skipped).
    ...                                     Recommended value: None for BTS without simulator, a list of configs otherwise.
    ...              - lua_config_file_path (str): absolute path to .lua or .cfg configuration file for simulator;
    ...                                            if None provided then simulator configuration file uploading will be skipped and BTS with simulator will not reach On Air state;
    ...                                            i.e. ${EXECDIR}/testsuite/Wroclaw/SISO/TestLines/7_16_UTE5GSISOAUTO005/LUA/SISOAUTO005_SBTS_master.lua
    ...                                            defaults to: None (simulator configuration file uploading will be skipped);
    ...                                            recommended value: None for BTS without simulator, .lua or .cfg file path otherwise
    ...              - alarms_for_second_log_collection (list(str)): fault names which detection will cause second snapshot collection after first log collection and 15 minutes of sleep
    ...                                                              defaults to: None (second snapshot collection will not be triggered);
    ...                                                              i.e ['No connection to unit', 'Radio autonomous reset as recovery action']
    ...                                                              Recommended value: None
    ...              - use_init_credentials_for_rmod_console (bool): defines whether initial credentials from init file should be used for RMOD serial console connections;
    ...                                                              Defaults to: False (taf.config.testline database credentials will be used);
    ...                                                              Recommended value: False
    ...              - oran_plugin_versions (dict): dictionary containing custom O-RAN plugin versions to install on RMODs,
    ...                                             where key is RMOD product code (string) and value is plugin version (string),
    ...                                             i.e. {'475701A.103': 'RFMPlugin_O-RU_NK_475701A-103_0017'}
    ...                                             Defaults to: None means the latest plugin version available on WFT will be used during plugin installation.
    ...                                             Recommended value: None

